    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Trea Turner** (78.64). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains our primary target for stolen base production, and his matchup against Lorenzen offers a massive boost; with a 14% platoon edge and favorable park factors, he is our highest-projected asset. Similarly, **Trea Turner** exploits a porous 5.32 xERA from Scherzer, compounding the efficiency of his #2 spot. While **Kyle Schwarber** (77.46) carries inherent risk against top-tier arms, his high xwOBA and favorable matchup against Scherzer cement his status as a \"Strong\" start for power production. We are also capitalizing on **Colt Keith** (66.37) and **Junior Caminero** (66.32), both of whom benefit from positive park and SP skill dynamics that elevate them above their base projections.\n\nOur most difficult roster management decision centered on the bench, where **Lars Nootbaar** (48.90) just missed the cut. Despite an elite 0.406 xwOBA, the optimizer favored the structural efficiency of our outfield trio and the positional versatility of our utility slot. While **Lars Nootbaar** offers high-quality contact, the limited cap space necessitates favoring players like **Carson Benge** (61.51), who nets a higher efficiency score due to his leadoff role and platoon advantage. We must also exercise caution with **Yordan Alvarez** (48.86); despite his elite 0.452 xwOBA, a difficult matchup against Detmers and a negative platoon split keep his projection in the marginal tier. We are monitoring all lineups closely, particularly for **Dillon Dingler** and **Gary Sanchez**, as catcher production remains a volatile variable in our daily cap management.",
